## Why This Is Asked

This question tests mastery of rope-like data structures for dynamic sequences with cut-paste operations while maintaining fast range queries.

## Key Concepts

- **Implicit treap / rope**: Uses position as the key rather than explicit values
- **Split and merge operations**: Fundamental primitives for manipulating segments
- **Augmented data**: size and range sum maintained at each node
- **Edge cases**: Properly handling when dest overlaps with [l, r]

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(v) {
    this.v = v;
    this.pr = Math.random();
    this.l = this.r = null;
    this.sz = 1;
    this.sum = v;
  }
}

function upd(t) {
  if (!t) return;
  t.sz = 1 + sz(t.l) + sz(t.r);
  t.sum = t.v + sum(t.l) + sum(t.r);
}

function split(t, k, l, r) {
  if (!t) return [null, null];
  if (sz(t.l) >= k) {
    let [a, b] = split(t.l, k, l, r);
    t.l = b; upd(t);
    return [a, t];
  } else {
    let [a, b] = split(t.r, k - sz(t.l) - 1, l, r);
    t.r = a; upd(t);
    return [t, b];
  }
}

function merge(a, b) {
  if (!a || !b) return a || b;
  if (a.pr < b.pr) {
    a.r = merge(a.r, b); upd(a); return a;
  } else {
    b.l = merge(a, b.l); upd(b); return b;
  }
}

function rangeSum(t, l, r) {
  let [a, bc] = split(t, l);
  let [b, c] = split(bc, r - l + 1);
  let res = sum(b);
  t = merge(a, merge(b, c));
  return res;
}

function moveSegment(t, l, r, dest) {
  let len = r - l + 1;
  let [a, bc] = split(t, l);
  let [b, c] = split(bc, len);
  t = merge(a, c);

  let pos = dest <= l ? dest : dest - len;
  let [x, y] = split(t, pos);\n  return merge(merge(x, b), y);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests mapping of high-level operations to a classic data-structure primitive (Fenwick tree) with dynamic growth.

## Key Concepts
- Fenwick tree (Binary Indexed Tree)
- 1-based indexing
- dynamic growth and delta updates
- handling duplicates in values

## Code Example
```javascript
class Fenwick {
  constructor(n){ this.n=n; this.ft=new Array(n+1).fill(0); this.arr=[] }
  append(v){ this.arr.push(v); const i=this.arr.length; this.add(i,v); }
  add(i,delta){ for(; i<=this.n; i+=i&-i) this.ft[i]+=delta; }
  update(i,v){ const delta=v-this.arr[i-1]; this.arr[i-1]=v; this.add(i,delta); }
  sum(i){ let s=0; for(; i>0; i-=i&-i) s+=this.ft[i]; return s; }
  range(l,r){ return this.sum(r)-this.sum(l-1); }
}
```

